          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<h2 id=\"observation-trajectory-linked-atlas\">Observation \u2194 Trajectory linked atlas</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Rebuild of the data-side analysis from <code>initial_report_v6.html</code>: every\nanchor frame (1 per second) yields an <strong>observation</strong> vector\n(proprioception + binned 120-step action history \u2014 what a policy\nconditions on) and a <strong>future-trajectory</strong> vector (binned next-180-step\naction chunk \u2014 what the demonstrator did). Both are embedded separately;\nthe two maps below share the same rows.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Brush the observation map, then click \"Update trajectory view\" \u2014 the\ntrajectory map lights up the chunks those observations produce.</strong> An\nobservation region that fans out to\n<em>multiple</em> trajectory regions is multimodal p(a|obs) \u2014 the report's\ncentral finding (adv \u2248 60% vs baseline \u2248 29% of obs neighborhoods\nmultimodal). Caveats: this uses UMAP (report: t-SNE) and no vision\nfeatures yet (see <code>vision.md</code>), so expect the adv \u226b baseline <em>gap</em>\nto reproduce, not the exact numbers.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
